WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.828
I woke up in our new apartment.

2
00:00:06.829 --> 00:00:10.674
My bed was shaking!

3
00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:15.308
The ceiling fan wiggled back and forth.

4
00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:20.204
Thump! My basketball rolled off a shelf.

5
00:00:20.205 --> 00:00:24.277
I put my pillow over my head.

6
00:00:24.278 --> 00:00:28.754
Finally the shaking stopped.

7
00:00:28.755 --> 00:00:31.623
Mom and Dad came to my room.

8
00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:34.848
"What was that?" I asked.

9
00:00:34.849 --> 00:00:38.099
"It was an earthquake," said Dad.

10
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.220
"Earthquakes occur in some parts of California.

11
00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:47.935
Let's make an earthquake plan tomorrow."

12
00:00:47.936 --> 00:00:51.760
The next morning Dad made breakfast.

13
00:00:51.761 --> 00:00:56.264
Mom and I researched earthquake safety on the computer.

14
00:00:56.265 --> 00:01:02.137
"If you're in bed, stay there with your head under a pillow," said Mom.

15
00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:05.481
"That's what I did," I said.

16
00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:08.588
"But that's because I was scared!"

17
00:01:08.589 --> 00:01:12.304
Mom laughed.

18
00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.241
I read the next part.

19
00:01:14.242 --> 00:01:20.007
"If you're inside, you should 'drop, cover, and hold on.'

20
00:01:20.008 --> 00:01:21.718
What does that mean?"

21
00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:27.133
"Drop to the floor and take cover under something sturdy.

22
00:01:27.134 --> 00:01:32.227
That way nothing will fall on you," said Mom.

23
00:01:32.228 --> 00:01:37.484
"This table is a good cover," said Dad, setting down pancakes.

24
00:01:37.485 --> 00:01:42.473
"If there's nothing sturdy nearby, drop down next to an inside wall.

25
00:01:42.474 --> 00:01:44.565
Stay away from windows.

26
00:01:44.566 --> 00:01:47.498
Broken glass could be dangerous.

27
00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:50.736
And don't use the elevator!"

28
00:01:50.737 --> 00:01:55.225
"Once you've found a cover, hold on to something sturdy.

29
00:01:55.226 --> 00:01:59.514
Put a hand over your eyes to protect them," said Mom.

30
00:01:59.515 --> 00:02:04.297
"If I'm outside, should I run inside?" I asked.

31
00:02:04.298 --> 00:02:10.485
"No. Move away from buildings, trees, and power lines," said Dad.

32
00:02:10.486 --> 00:02:14.882
"Then drop to the ground until the shaking stops."

33
00:02:14.883 --> 00:02:18.514
"We'll make a disaster kit," said Mom.

34
00:02:18.515 --> 00:02:24.089
"Aftershocks can happen even days after an earthquake."

35
00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:30.385
At the store Mom bought a flashlight, a radio, and extra batteries.

36
00:02:30.386 --> 00:02:37.388
I got bottled water and enough canned food to last three days.

37
00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:48.445
But I didn't get any peas—yuck!

38
00:02:48.446 --> 00:02:53.166
Back at home, Dad put tools in our disaster kit.

39
00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:59.093
Mom added first aid supplies and extra clothes.

40
00:02:59.094 --> 00:03:03.147
Suddenly the floor trembled!

41
00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:06.896
We dropped to the floor and took cover under the table.

42
00:03:06.897 --> 00:03:10.949
I held a table leg and covered my eyes.

43
00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.499
I wasn't too scared this time.

44
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:24.177
I knew what to do!

